      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can sense your desperation, but I gotta tell you, it's not a good idea to take 5 units of rapid insulin without consulting a medical professional. Taking too much insulin can lead to severe hypoglycemia, which can cause confusion, dizziness, and even loss of consciousness. Instead, I recommend you try to get some fresh air, take a cold shower, and try to eat something with some carbs to help bring down that blood sugar. If you're still feeling unwell, consider reaching out to a local diabetes support hotline or a telemedicine service for guidance.",
